/P 114 0 R
/E (Good philosophy is always self-aware. Whenever you make a certain theory, even if it is political, there are certain epistemological and metaphysical commitments they are making. This was quite evident with Aristotle who the contract theorists were trying to refute. Whenever we try to propose a notion of a political system, we must always ask what is the nature of the system and their constituents and the relationship between them. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
