162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (So, reason is a requisite for being a participant. What exactly is reason here? To understand this, we need to grasp a better sense of human nature. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (Locke considers sensation as the only source of knowledge. All our knowledge is provided to us by sense-experience. Since everything we can know is provided to us by our senses, therefore, the participant does not know anything before they can sense things. This is why all humans are tabula rasa or blank slates prior to sense experience. Since knowledge is acquired from sense-experience, we are not born with the knowledge of absolute truths. Instead, with sense experience, we expand our knowledge of truths and modify them according to our sense-experience.  )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (This is tandem with his notion of tolerance. The suppression of idea hinders knowledge because there is a possible sense-experience we may miss out. Locke despite being a devout Christian, advocated for the separation of the church and the State. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
