/E (The State of Nature:)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (The two-stage contract theory ensures that since government and society are distinct, the elimination of the government will not result in the elimination of society. A government being answerable to its participants can be overturned by the society if deemed to violate their natural rights. From this we have the theory of popular sovereignty. The government is limited in its power because it is only allowed to enforce natural laws by the participants through popular consent. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
