/P 121 0 R
/E (The combination of sense-experience and natural rights lead to the psychological explanation of human nature. Consistent with Hobbes, since sense-experience is the only source of knowledge we have, our knowledge of moral truths must also be acquired through our sensations and most importantly, be observable through sensations. How do we know something is wrong? When we do not feel good about it i.e. it causes us some type of psycho-physical pain. We find something good when we find it pleasurable. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
